   "answer": "Many tunings of that era gave each key its own colour: near-pure thirds in C, edgier ones in keys with many sharps or flats. Composers chose keys knowing it. Equal temperament makes every key identical, so a key picked for its sweetness sounds like any other. It erases a colour the score assumed.",
   "move": "Whichever side you took, it turns on what is knowable about the tuning composers heard.",
